IDEA 1: Concept Coverage (untested) — From cached student block-6 patch outputs \(Z\), form signed channels \(X=[\max(Z,0),\max(-Z,0)]\); fit rank-6 nonnegative matrix factorization \(X\approx HW\) using 15 updates, and normalize each concept map: \(u_{ic}=H_{ic}/(\sum_jH_{jc}+\epsilon)\).  
Starting with \(S=\varnothing\), repeatedly score unselected patches by \(\sum_c\log[1+u_{ic}/(1/196+\sum_{j\in S}u_{jc})]\), keeping exactly \(\lfloor K\rfloor\); this gives diminishing returns to already represented concepts and limits domination by spatially extensive background concepts.  
— basis: Collins, Achanta & Süsstrunk, [Deep Feature Factorization for Concept Discovery, ECCV 2018](https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.10206); signed channels and budgeted concept coverage are proposed adaptations.  
— closest prior token-pruning work and difference: [Token Pooling](https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.03860) minimizes feature reconstruction error through clustering; this selects original patches through normalized coverage of interpretable concept maps.  
— extra FLOPs: approximately 0.03–0.12 GFLOPs/image for width 192–384, including factorization and greedy selection; no additional student forward or gradients.

IDEA 2: Sparse-Residual Counterfactual Attribution (untested) — Scale cached block-6 patch features \(Z\) by their median norm \(a\), giving \(X\); approximately minimize \(\frac12\|X-L-E\|_F^2+0.1\sum_i\|E_i\|_2\), with \(\operatorname{rank}(L)\le4\), using 10 alternating randomized rank-4 approximations and rowwise soft-thresholding.  
Score \(s_i=|\nabla_{Z_i}(z_0-z_1)^\top(Z_i-aL_i)|\), where \(z_0,z_1\) are student logits; keep the top \(\lfloor K\rfloor\): a first-order explanation of replacing each patch’s internal representation with its fitted common component, using `autograd.grad(..., retain_graph=True)` without parameter `.grad` writes.  
— inspired by: Xu, Caramanis & Sanghavi, [Robust PCA via Outlier Pursuit, NeurIPS 2010, arXiv:1010.4237](https://arxiv.org/abs/1010.4237).  
— why it transfers: Whole-vector outlier separation directly suggests isolating unusual bird representations from repeated scenery, while directional attribution tests their decision relevance; this background-subspace assumption and the fixed-rank approximation require validation.  
— queries tried: unsupervised object discovery feature graph normalized cut foreground background spectral eigenvectors; low rank sparse decomposition background foreground moving objects outlier pursuit; experimental design subset measurements preserve information determinant volume sampling; invariant prediction causal features environment interventions texture shape bias; neural representation concept completeness sufficient explanations information bottleneck; optimal experimental design volume sampling diverse subset measurements paper.  
— closest prior token-pruning work and difference: [GeoPrune](https://aclanthology.org/2026.findings-emnlp.1913/) ranks residual norms after dominant-component removal; this robustly separates patch outliers and ranks their counterfactual effect on the student’s class margin.  
— extra FLOPs: approximately 1–3 GFLOPs/image including the suffix gradient and decomposition; neither proposal has established Full-KD accuracy/WGA proximity or superiority over all six baselines at matched K.